Subject: Expose a window's sandbox engine, app id and instance id

A window whose client connected through a wp_security_context_v1 listener
gains three constant properties, sandboxEngine, sandboxAppId and
sandboxInstanceId, read from the client connection, and the decoration
bridge passes them to KDecoration3's DecoratedWindowPrivateV5, so a
decoration can mark a sandboxed window. An X11 window reads as unsandboxed:
its surface belongs to Xwayland. Needs the KDecoration3 change that adds
DecoratedWindowPrivateV5, and the sandbox-policy patch that keeps the engine
and instance id on the client connection.

